WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.601
-Welcome back to
The Tonight Show, everybody.

00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:03.968
I'm Steve Higgins
and it's time to play...

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:11.100
♪♪

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.734
Well, well, well. Let's meet
our contestants. To my left,

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:15.968
he's an Emmy- and Tony-winning
actor

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:17.667
who stars in the new movie
"Beau Is Afraid,"

00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:19.968
in theaters April 21st.

00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:21.467
Give it up for Nathan Lane!

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:25.968
Oh, my goodness.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:28.234
Brilliant. Nathan, your partner
this evening

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:30.767
is the host of NBC's
"The Tonight Show"

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:33.567
and Grammy -- oh, Grammy
Award-winning musician

00:00:33.567 --> 00:00:34.934
Jimmy Fallon!

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:38.734
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:38.734 --> 00:00:40.467
Oh, my gosh.

00:00:40.467 --> 00:00:41.934
Well, your first opponent
is a member

00:00:41.934 --> 00:00:44.934
of the legendary Roots crew.
Say hello to Questlove!

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:46.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.334
-Okay.

00:00:48.334 --> 00:00:49.634
-He's just a member of
The Roots.

00:00:49.634 --> 00:00:51.334
You won a Grammy.
-I did win a Grammy Award.

00:00:51.334 --> 00:00:52.767
-Yeah, you did. Wow.

00:00:52.767 --> 00:00:54.467
-Do you know what it's like
to win an award, Quest? Yeah.

00:00:54.467 --> 00:00:56.367
-One day I'll find out, man.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:00:56.367 --> 00:00:57.801
-And Quest's partner stars in

00:00:57.801 --> 00:01:00.400
the Apple TV+ series
"Schmigadoon!"

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.300
Season two premieres April 5th.
It's Dove Cameron!

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:08.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.534
The rules of the game
are very simple.

00:01:09.534 --> 00:01:12.667
I will give
each of you a password

00:01:12.667 --> 00:01:14.200
and then you are
to give a one-word clue.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.901
That's one word only to get your
partner to guess the password.

00:01:17.901 --> 00:01:21.767
The team with the most points
after four words wins.

00:01:21.767 --> 00:01:23.701
First clue goes to Jimmy
and Questlove.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:26.667
-Now, before we start, I'd like
to set some ground rules.

00:01:26.667 --> 00:01:28.901
-Oh, boy.
-You know, I've played

00:01:28.901 --> 00:01:31.000
many games with Jimmy
over the years,

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.033
and it always turns ugly.
-Oh, my God.

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.267
I'm very competitive.
-He starts out as

00:01:36.267 --> 00:01:39.501
very happy-go-lucky,
"everything is awesome" Jimmy.

00:01:39.501 --> 00:01:42.567
And it turns into
very competitive

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.601
and a lot of misplaced anger
Jimmy.

00:01:44.601 --> 00:01:45.868
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:48.400
-I do not do that.
-Which I find very triggering.

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:50.667
So I just wanted to say

00:01:50.667 --> 00:01:54.434
as we watch
Western civilization

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:58.534
and democracy disintegrate
before our eyes,

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:00.133
a little game of "Password"

00:02:00.133 --> 00:02:03.534
is not the most important
thing in the world

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.434
and that no matter
who wins or who loses,

00:02:06.434 --> 00:02:09.667
you're still a very special boy
and we all love you.

00:02:09.667 --> 00:02:17.467
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:17.467 --> 00:02:20.734
Now let's play the [bleep] game,
Jimmy.

00:02:20.734 --> 00:02:22.634
-Jimmy and Quest,
you got the first clue.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:24.200
-The password is...

00:02:25.267 --> 00:02:27.868
-Start us off.
-Oh, come on.

00:02:27.868 --> 00:02:29.467
-Ooh!

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.367
-I'm in trouble already.
-No.

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:35.968
-It's me who's in trouble.

00:02:36.968 --> 00:02:38.234
You sure you want to go first?

00:02:38.234 --> 00:02:40.367
-Yeah. No, you first.
-Hmm.

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.000
Tulips?

00:02:50.033 --> 00:02:52.200
-Tiptoe?

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.767
-Quest.

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:55.968
Worth 5 points.

00:02:56.834 --> 00:02:58.434
-10, brah.
-Danny 10, brah.

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:01.567
Uh, I hope this is
the right color.

00:03:03.434 --> 00:03:05.734
Yellow.
-Easter?

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:08.167
-No.

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:09.400
-What are the passwords
so far?

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:12.367
-Yellow and tulips.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.667
-Flowers.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:21.734
-Flowers.

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.067
Um...

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:29.033
-Yes. Yes. Yes. Yes.
Yes. Say it. Say it.

00:03:29.033 --> 00:03:31.601
-Holland?
-Yes. Holland.

00:03:31.601 --> 00:03:33.200
Holland.
-Holland. For tulips.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.167
-Really?
-Wow.

00:03:34.167 --> 00:03:35.834
-No?
-Alright.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:39.133
-You see what I'm talking about,
ladies and gentlemen?

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:41.234
He's already turned on me.

00:03:41.234 --> 00:03:42.434
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:43.934
Already.
-Holland! Holland!

00:03:43.934 --> 00:03:47.367
-We got Holland. We got tulips.
-Tulips and flowers.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:48.868
-Yeah.
-I've only heard this

00:03:48.868 --> 00:03:52.167
in one song, and I hope you knew
this reference.

00:03:52.167 --> 00:03:53.934
-Okay.
-Um...

00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:57.934
And I hope we can pay
for the publishing.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:05.267
♪ Flow-ers ♪

00:04:05.267 --> 00:04:07.000
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:09.834
-And the reference was lost
on the entire audience.

00:04:09.834 --> 00:04:12.000
[ Sad tuba ]
-Shut up, tuba!

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:18.267
-I honestly have no idea.
Spring?

00:04:18.267 --> 00:04:19.868
-Spring. Spring.

00:04:22.601 --> 00:04:24.200
-Springtime.
-Oh.

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:26.934
-Hitler.

00:04:26.934 --> 00:04:31.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.601
-Alright, score 0-0.
The word was "daffodil."

00:04:34.601 --> 00:04:36.100
-Ah!

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:37.767
-The password is...

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.534
-Dove, you are first.
[ Audience ohhs ]

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:42.534
Oh, my God.

00:04:42.534 --> 00:04:45.033
